<title>USA: MasterCard caps debit card liability.</title>
<headline>MasterCard caps debit card liability.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>MasterCard International, an association of financial service companies that issue credit cards, said Wednesday its U.S. member banks voted to cap liability for unauthorized use of U.S.-issued MasterCard-branded debit cards at $50.</p>
<p>MasterCard International said that the previous limitation was set by U.S. regulation and ranged from $50 to an unlimited amount.</p>
<p>MasterCard said the change only protects debit cardholders with cards that have the MasterCard logo.</p>
<p>Debit cards deduct funds from a cardholder's savings or checking account.</p>
</text>
